{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And now</b> — The opinion of many commentators: that this concerns the future, in the days of the Messiah, and the proof: 'And you, Bethlehem Ephrathah.' R. Moses the Kohen said: that it speaks of the Second Temple, and 'the ruler' is Zerubbabel, and the meaning of 'Arise and thresh' is like 'Who are you, O great mountain' [Zechariah 4:7], for Zerubbabel was of the descendants of Jeconiah, and it is written of him: 'and shall rule on his throne.'" "<b>Be profaned</b> — like 'the deceitful land cannot bear' [Job 24:25], using the root חנף."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The cross-references to 'And you, Bethlehem Ephrathah' and 'and shall rule on his throne' allude respectively to Micah 5:1 and Zechariah 6:13 (the latter applied to Zerubbabel); Ibn Ezra cites them by phrase rather than by verse citation.", 1 "The Hebrew word תחנף (from חנף) in the lemma is here glossed by Ibn Ezra with a phrase from Job 24:25; I rendered the Job phrase by its sense as Ibn Ezra deploys it."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:57.901232169Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}